---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="SDA Strategic Divestment Advisory | SDA Home Choices" description="We help owners, boards, lenders and appointed advisers assess the commercial position of an SDA property or portfolio and determine a practical way forward.">
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="SDA Strategic Divestment Advisory"
    title="Know where you stand. Decide what comes next."
    standfirst="Should you hold, improve, reposition or sell your SDA assets? We help owners, boards, lenders and appointed advisers assess the commercial position of an SDA property or portfolio, compare realistic options and determine a practical way forward. The starting point is your situation, not an assumption that selling is the right answer."
  />
  <section class="pagehead-cta"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="btn b1" href="/contact-us/">Discuss your SDA asset strategy</a>
    </div>
    <p class="lead-secondary">Already ready to sell? <a href="/sda-property-and-portfolio-sales/">Explore Property &amp; Portfolio Sales</a>.</p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section advisory-flow advisory-flow-top">
    <div class="wrap advisory-lead prose">
      <h2>Before you choose an exit, understand your options.</h2>
      <p>A decision about SDA property can involve more than an expected sale price. You may need to understand why income is below expectations, whether further expenditure is justified, what a buyer would need to see, or whether holding the asset is a credible alternative to selling. Our advisory service brings these questions together in a structured commercial assessment. We examine the available evidence, make assumptions explicit and identify the decisions that matter most. The outcome is a clearer basis for action, not simply another opinion on what the property might be worth.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="advisory-grid-heading">For decisions that need more than a market appraisal.</h2>
      <div class="audience-grid">
        <div class="audience-card">
          <span class="card-mark"></span>
          <h3>Owners and developers reviewing their next move</h3>
          <p>You may be considering an exit, facing ongoing vacancy, reviewing your portfolio or deciding whether to commit more capital. We help assess the options before further time or money is invested.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="audience-card">
          <span class="card-mark"></span>
          <h3>Boards and property-owning organisations</h3>
          <p>You may need a documented basis for retaining, repositioning or divesting property holdings. We help clarify the commercial implications, the evidence gaps and the practical steps associated with each pathway.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="audience-card">
          <span class="card-mark"></span>
          <h3>Lenders, receivers and administrators</h3>
          <p>You may need an SDA-specific view of an asset's performance, marketability and potential disposal options. We provide commercial property support alongside the appointed professional team.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section advisory-paper advisory-paper-factors">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="advisory-grid-heading advisory-grid-heading-dark">We assess the factors that shape the decision.</h2>
      <div class="factor-grid">
        <div class="factor-card">
          <h3>Actual income and operating performance</h3>
          <p>We review the available income records, occupancy information and operating costs to understand the current position. Actual receipts are distinguished from projected income, funding assumptions and fully occupied scenarios.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="factor-card">
          <h3>Local market conditions</h3>
          <p>We examine relevant demand evidence, competing accommodation and the provider environment. The purpose is to assess the asset in its own market, not to assume that national SDA demand translates into local occupancy.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="factor-card">
          <h3>Provider and property arrangements</h3>
          <p>We review the commercial implications of available leases, management agreements, fees and operating arrangements. Matters requiring legal interpretation are identified for review by your legal advisers.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="factor-card">
          <h3>Saleability and buyer requirements</h3>
          <p>We consider how a prospective buyer may assess the asset, which uncertainties could affect an offer and what information or preparation may be needed before approaching the market.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="factor-card">
          <h3>Holding, improvement and exit scenarios</h3>
          <p>We compare relevant pathways using explicit assumptions about timing, costs, income and execution risk. Where appropriate, this may include considering alternative-use potential, subject to planning, legal and valuation advice.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section advisory-flow advisory-flow-deliverables">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="advisory-grid-heading">A commercial recommendation you can act on.</h2>
      <p class="advisory-grid-intro">The scope is tailored to the decision you need to make. Depending on the engagement, your written advice may include:</p>
      <div class="deliverable-grid">
        <div class="deliverable-card">
          <span class="step-no">01</span>
          <h3>A clear assessment of the current position</h3>
          <p>A consolidated view of the asset or portfolio, its documented performance, material commercial risks and outstanding information requirements.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="deliverable-card">
          <span class="step-no">02</span>
          <h3>A comparison of realistic options</h3>
          <p>An assessment of the relevant pathways, including the assumptions, costs, timing considerations and dependencies associated with each.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="deliverable-card">
          <span class="step-no">03</span>
          <h3>A recommended course of action</h3>
          <p>A reasoned recommendation explaining what should happen next, why that pathway is preferred and what could change the conclusion.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="deliverable-card">
          <span class="step-no">04</span>
          <h3>A practical implementation roadmap</h3>
          <p>Prioritised actions, further information requirements and the specialist input needed to progress the recommendation. Where a sale is appropriate, this can include a sale-readiness plan and recommended approach to market.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section advisory-paper advisory-paper-narrative">
    <div class="wrap advisory-lead prose">
      <h2>The recommendation may be to sell. It may also be to wait.</h2>
      <p>An immediate sale is one possible outcome, not the default. The assessment may support retaining an asset, addressing specific operating issues, preparing for a later exit, selling selected properties or undertaking a broader divestment. We explain the conditions each option depends on. Where a strategy relies on improved occupancy, additional funding, renegotiated agreements or further capital, those dependencies are made clear rather than presented as assured outcomes. The objective is to help you make a defensible commercial decision with a realistic understanding of the trade-offs.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="wrap advisory-pair">
      <div class="prose advisory-pair-item">
        <h2>Specialist property insight for complex or time-sensitive situations.</h2>
        <p>For lenders, receivers, administrators and restructuring advisers, our role is to help establish what the SDA asset represents commercially, and what the available pathways may involve. This can include reviewing the information needed to assess a disposal, considering immediate sale against a holding or stabilisation scenario, and identifying property-specific issues that may affect timing or buyer interest. We work alongside the appointed insolvency practitioners, legal advisers, valuers and operational providers. Our contribution is SDA-focused commercial property assessment and, where separately appointed, sale execution. Any proposed transition should also account for existing residents and operating arrangements, with the appropriate providers and advisers involved.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="prose advisory-pair-item">
        <h2>A defined advisory engagement, not a commitment to sell.</h2>
        <p>We agree the scope, fees, information requirements and deliverables before work begins. The advisory engagement is designed to stand on its own. You receive the agreed assessment and recommendations without being required to proceed with a sale through SDAHC. Where a sale is recommended and you wish to appoint us, the transaction mandate and its terms are agreed separately.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section advisory-flow advisory-flow-faq">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Common questions about SDA advisory.</h2>
      <div class="faq">
        <details>
          <summary>Is this service only for distressed or underperforming assets?</summary>
          <p>No. It is also relevant to owners of performing assets who are considering capital recycling, portfolio changes or a planned exit. The service is driven by the decision required, not only by financial pressure.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Is this a formal property valuation?</summary>
          <p>No. Our work provides commercial assessment, market positioning and strategic advice within the agreed scope. A formal valuation, legal opinion, tax advice or insolvency advice must be provided by the appropriately qualified professional.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Can SDAHC help implement the recommendation?</summary>
          <p>Where agreed, we can assist with sale preparation, coordinate relevant specialist input and manage a subsequent sales process under a separate mandate. Operational, legal and funding-related actions remain with the appropriate providers and advisers.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section advisory-flow advisory-cta-section">
    <div class="wrap advisory-cta-inner">
      <h2>Before committing to a sale, or more capital, get a clearer commercial picture.</h2>
      <p>Tell us about your property or portfolio, the decision you are facing and any timing constraints. We will discuss an advisory scope suited to the situation.</p>
      <p><a class="btn b1" href="/contact-us/">Discuss an advisory engagement</a></p>
      <p class="cta-note">Confidential enquiries from owners, boards, lenders and appointed advisers.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
:root{
  --advisory-depth:.85;
  --advisory-flow-top:var(--navy);
  --advisory-flow-mid:var(--slate);
}

/* hero: same layered gradient/glow recipe as About/Sales, scoped to this page only */
:global(section.pagehead.pagehead){background:var(--navy);overflow:hidden}
:global(section.pagehead)::after{content:"";position:absolute;inset:0;z-index:0;opacity:var(--advisory-depth);background:radial-gradient(120% 130% at 12% 0%,#0b4a86 0%,rgba(11,74,134,0) 55%),radial-gradient(100% 120% at 100% 100%,rgba(4,118,217,.42) 0%,rgba(4,118,217,0) 58%),linear-gradient(160deg,var(--navy2) 0%,var(--navy) 78%)}
:global(section.pagehead .wrap){position:relative;z-index:1}

/* navy flow bands: same layered recipe as About/Sales, one shared strength dial */
.advisory-flow{position:relative;overflow:hidden;background:var(--navy)}
.advisory-flow::after{content:"";position:absolute;inset:0;z-index:0;opacity:var(--advisory-depth);background:radial-gradient(120% 130% at 12% 0%,#0b4a86 0%,rgba(11,74,134,0) 55%),radial-gradient(100% 120% at 100% 100%,rgba(4,118,217,.42) 0%,rgba(4,118,217,0) 58%),linear-gradient(160deg,var(--navy2) 0%,var(--navy) 78%)}
.advisory-flow>*{position:relative;z-index:1}

.advisory-flow-top::before{content:"";position:absolute;inset:0;z-index:0;background:linear-gradient(180deg,var(--advisory-flow-top) 0%,var(--advisory-flow-mid) 78%,color-mix(in srgb,var(--navy) 45%,var(--paper)) 100%)}
.advisory-flow-deliverables::before{content:"";position:absolute;inset:0;z-index:0;background:linear-gradient(180deg,color-mix(in srgb,var(--navy) 70%,var(--paper)) 0%,var(--navy) 14%,var(--navy) 100%)}
.advisory-flow-faq::before{content:"";position:absolute;inset:0;z-index:0;background:linear-gradient(180deg,color-mix(in srgb,var(--navy) 75%,var(--paper)) 0%,var(--navy) 12%,var(--navy) 100%)}

/* paper bands: AA-checked overrides for the shared .prose colours, same values used on About/Sales */
.advisory-paper{position:relative;overflow:hidden;background:var(--paper)}
.advisory-paper .prose{color:var(--slate)}
.advisory-paper .prose h2{color:var(--navy)}
.advisory-paper .prose strong{color:var(--navy)}
.advisory-paper .prose a{color:var(--navy2)}
.advisory-paper-factors::before{content:"";position:absolute;inset:0;z-index:0;background:linear-gradient(180deg,var(--navy) 0%,var(--paper) 18%,var(--paper) 100%)}
.advisory-paper-narrative::before{content:"";position:absolute;inset:0;z-index:0;background:linear-gradient(180deg,var(--navy) 0%,var(--paper) 14%,var(--paper) 82%,color-mix(in srgb,var(--navy) 55%,var(--paper)) 100%)}
.advisory-paper>*{position:relative;z-index:1}

/* shared lead paragraph and paired-paragraph layout, wider than a narrow floating column */
.advisory-lead{max-width:78ch;margin:0 auto;padding:0}
.advisory-lead.prose{margin-bottom:56px}
.advisory-pair{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:48px;align-items:start}
.advisory-pair-item{max-width:none;padding:0;margin:0}
@media(max-width:860px){.advisory-pair{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:40px}}

.advisory-grid-heading{font-family:var(--serif);font-weight:600;color:#fff;font-size:clamp(24px,3.2vw,34px);line-height:1.15;margin:0 0 40px;text-align:center}
.advisory-grid-heading-dark{color:var(--navy)}
.advisory-grid-intro{font-family:var(--sans);color:var(--pale);font-size:16px;text-align:center;max-width:60ch;margin:-16px auto 36px}

/* the three audience segments: uniform cards, unnumbered, a small consistent keyline marker */
.audience-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:24px;align-items:stretch}
.audience-card{display:flex;flex-direction:column;height:100%;padding:28px 24px;border:1px solid color-mix(in srgb,var(--pale) 18%,transparent);border-radius:10px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.05);transition:transform .22s ease,border-color .22s ease,background .22s ease}
.audience-card:hover{transform:translateY(-4px);border-color:color-mix(in srgb,var(--blue) 55%,transparent);background:rgba(255,255,255,.08)}
.audience-card .card-mark{display:block;width:28px;height:3px;background:var(--blue);margin-bottom:16px;border-radius:2px}
.audience-card h3{font-family:var(--serif);font-weight:600;color:#fff;font-size:clamp(17px,1.6vw,19px);line-height:1.25;margin:0 0 12px}
.audience-card p{font-family:var(--sans);color:#fff;font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.6;margin:0}
@media(max-width:980px){.audience-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:22px}}
@media(max-width:560px){.audience-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.audience-card{transition:background .22s ease,border-color .22s ease}.audience-card:hover{transform:none}}

/* the five assessment factors: uniform paper-context cards, three then two centred */
.factor-grid{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;justify-content:center;gap:24px}
.factor-card{display:flex;flex-direction:column;flex:1 1 calc(33.333% - 16px);min-width:240px;max-width:calc(33.333% - 16px);padding:28px 24px;border:1px solid color-mix(in srgb,var(--navy) 14%,transparent);border-radius:10px;background:#fff;box-shadow:0 12px 30px rgba(0,10,25,.08);transition:transform .22s ease,border-color .22s ease,box-shadow .22s ease}
.factor-card:hover{transform:translateY(-4px);border-color:var(--blue);box-shadow:0 16px 36px rgba(0,10,25,.14)}
.factor-card h3{font-family:var(--serif);font-weight:600;color:var(--navy);font-size:clamp(17px,1.6vw,19px);line-height:1.25;margin:0 0 12px}
.factor-card p{font-family:var(--sans);color:var(--slate);font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.6;margin:0}
@media(max-width:900px){.factor-card{flex:1 1 calc(50% - 12px);max-width:calc(50% - 12px)}}
@media(max-width:560px){.factor-card{flex:1 1 100%;max-width:100%}}
@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.factor-card{transition:box-shadow .22s ease,border-color .22s ease}.factor-card:hover{transform:none}}

/* the four deliverables: same numbered-card recipe as the Sales process steps */
.deliverable-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:24px;align-items:stretch}
.deliverable-card{display:flex;flex-direction:column;height:100%;padding:28px 24px;border:1px solid color-mix(in srgb,var(--pale) 18%,transparent);border-radius:10px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.05);transition:transform .22s ease,border-color .22s ease,background .22s ease}
.deliverable-card:hover{transform:translateY(-4px);border-color:color-mix(in srgb,var(--blue) 55%,transparent);background:rgba(255,255,255,.08)}
.deliverable-card .step-no{display:block;font-family:var(--cond);font-weight:600;font-size:13px;letter-spacing:.1em;color:#fff;margin-bottom:14px}
.deliverable-card h3{font-family:var(--serif);font-weight:600;color:#fff;font-size:clamp(16.5px,1.6vw,18.5px);line-height:1.25;margin:0 0 12px}
.deliverable-card p{font-family:var(--sans);color:#fff;font-size:14px;line-height:1.6;margin:0}
@media(max-width:980px){.deliverable-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:22px}}
@media(max-width:560px){.deliverable-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.deliverable-card{transition:background .22s ease,border-color .22s ease}.deliverable-card:hover{transform:none}}

/* closing CTA, tidy centred placement with the same depth as the hero */
.advisory-cta-inner{text-align:center;max-width:64ch;margin:0 auto}
.advisory-cta-inner h2{font-family:var(--serif);font-weight:600;color:#fff;font-size:clamp(26px,3.4vw,38px);line-height:1.12;margin:0}
.advisory-cta-inner p{color:var(--pale);margin:20px 0 0}
.advisory-cta-inner .cta-note{color:var(--pale);font-size:13px}
</style>
